==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|statut}}, from {{der|en|fro|statut}}, from {{der|en|LL.|statutum||a statute}}, neuter singular of {{der|en|la|statutus}}, past participle of {{m|la|statuō||I set up, establish}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstæt͡ʃuːt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-statute.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A written [[law]] or [[ordinance]] passed by a [[legislative body]]. {{defdate|from ca. 1300s}}
# A [[rule]] of an [[organization]] or [[institution]]. {{defdate|from 1389}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|biblical}} A law or [[decree]] made by a [[sovereign]], or by [[God]].
# {{lb|en|law|historical}} A (theoretical) type of [[statutory]] [[law]] specified as regulating a [[person]] or [[thing]]. {{defdate|from 1791}}
## Legal status of being [[subject]] to this.
# {{lb|en|historical}} A [[statute fair]]. {{defdate|from before 1600}}

